Z||000000||BlackARROW||09-05-2001||12:42 PM||||I have heard of a Speed Cut-Off on Fiero, like at 180 km/h (about 113mph) or maybe is it just  Canadian Restriction?  (just like the new Cadillac are blocked at 180kph - but if you set your speed display in MPH - it blocks it at 180 mph...  so stupid... hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>Anyway, I have heard that PowerChips was overcoming that speed cut-off (other than giving more fuel/air and blablabla)  What do you know of such Chips?  Still available?<P>I have a 2m4, but didn't get to that point yet.  Though my speedometer cannot very tell me where I am (I am getting close to the 0 though... a complete turn would be a goal  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )  The cut-off must be at the speed, not the RPM, maybe on the latest year models? Or maybe just on the V6 models? What I am expecting from that cut-off is a motor stall or something - which I didn't get yet - or would it be just that the speed will stop at that point without a stall?<P>Anyway, I am just trying to get that info for the knowledge of all.  I know, speeding is not right children - but once in a while, it helps stabilizing my arterial pressure.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Black-&gt;<BR>'85 2m4 (gadgetered)||||reg||1
