Z||000002||Voytek||09-05-2001||02:43 PM||||I don't think it's the computer that doesn't let you go any faster.  I've had an '85 SE 4-cyl.  I could also get it pretty close to 0 (top speed of around 170 kph).  I believe it's the 94 HP engine that just won't do anything better.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Brandon86SE||09-05-2001||04:29 PM||||Ya, as far as I can tell, my car isn't governed, and it's bone stock.  I've never had it cut out on me at high RPM's or high speed.  Although, I don't usually let it get into red line for very long, but I have ran it over 200kph, so I can tell you it's not governed at 180kph anyway.<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||09-05-2001||07:33 PM||||No Fiero is top speed governed.<P>88s Don't even have a rev limiter....<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000005||terryk||09-05-2001||07:35 PM||||Many 85's were and the 86-88 have the option in the code but it's disabled. I think some early 86's might have it set.<P>All V6's have the ability to speed and RPM limit, but they weren't set on most 86-88. Some early 86's might be set. I have an 85 manual that is set for both RPM and MPH.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||jelly2m8||09-05-2001||07:51 PM|||| <A HREF="http://medlem.tripodnet.nu/need4speed/class7-1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://medlem.tripodnet.nu/need4speed/class7-1.html</A> <P>look in here at listing # 12, Fieros aren't speed limited, but apparently the pre-88 V6's have a rev limiter at 6k or so.<P>I've hit 5500 rpm in 5th gear already, and the car was still pulling. The speed listed on that URL was obtained using a scan tool reading. Althought the 230kph pic shows arount 4500 on the tach, the actual rpm's was 5200~ at 230 kph. i sent the guy the 5200 rpm shot too, but I guess he posted the wrong one. I will post the 5200 rpm shot if someone tells me how to attach pics.<p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 09-05-2001).]||||reg||1
