Z||000012||Butter||09-07-2001||11:23 AM||||Hey Yall,<BR>Yes my 2m4 was speed limited back when I had the 2.5 in it.  It went into what I believe GM called Scatter Fire.  From what I've picked up on the subject, the computer is designed to reach this condition if it was set up with regular tires.  Most tires are rated at about 108 mph and still be safe.  So, a safety was designed to not let the engine go past that speed.  If the car come out with performace tires (high speed radials) then the scatter fire condition was not designed in the computer.  The Fiero I had was an 84 and would reach about 110 to 115 on a down hill stretch before it kicked out.||||reg||1
